            "role": "tenant",
            "name": "Hannah Osei"
          },
          "body": "Morning! Nothing dramatic - there's a tiny leak under the kitchen sink. I noticed a damp patch on the cabinet floor yesterday and put a takeaway tub under the pipe. It catches maybe a teaspoon a day. No rush at all, whenever someone is next in the area.",
          "occurredAt": "2025-11-03T09:12:00Z"
        },
        {
          "eventId": "case-04-event-2",
          "cursor": 6,
          "actor": {
            "id": "tenant-hannah",
            "role": "tenant",
            "name": "Hannah Osei"
          },
          "body": "It looks like it's from the joint where the curved bit meets the straight pipe going into the wall. Cabinet floor is just surface-damp, wiped it dry this morning and it's fine. Honestly it's a dribble.",
          "occurredAt": "2025-11-03T10:47:00Z"
        },
        {
          "eventId": "case-04-event-3",
          "cursor": 9,
          "actor": {
            "id": "tenant-hannah",
            "role": "tenant",
            "name": "Hannah Osei"
          },
          "body": "Quick update - it's dripping a bit faster now, the tub was about a third full this morning rather than a puddle at the bottom. Still not scary but thought you should know. Any word on the plumber?",
          "occurredAt": "2025-11-05T08:31:00Z"
        },
        {
